---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="One seeded 160 second trace: a heartbeat per second, a 6 second GC pause at 60 s, a packet-loss blip at 100 s, a real crash at 140 s. Pick a detector and a jitter level.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>Fixed timeout 2 s</b> and <b>High</b> jitter. It catches the crash after about <b>2.1 s</b> but raises <b>6 false alarms</b>: four from plain jitter, plus the pause and the blip.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>Phi accrual, threshold 8</b>. False alarms drop to <b>2</b> (a warm-up alarm in the first seconds and the 6 s pause) and detection takes about <b>4.4 s</b>. The 3 s gap of the blip no longer trips it: the window now holds the spikes and the 6 s pause, so the learned standard deviation is large and phi 8 needs about 4 s of silence.</li>
    <li>Try <b>Fixed timeout 10 s</b>: <b>0</b> false alarms, but the crash is found after <b>10.1 s</b>. Then try <b>SWIM, 5 s suspicion</b>: the pause is suspected and then <b>refuted</b>, so no false verdict, at about <b>7 s</b>. Set <b>Blip reaches</b> to the whole segment and one more suspicion is raised (3 becomes 4), because the indirect probes no longer get through.</li>
    <li>Drag the <b>Playhead</b> (or press Play) to read the suspicion value at any moment, and look at the curves: no setting finds the crash in under about 6 s with zero false alarms.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg fd" data-fd>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Detector
        <select class="pg-in" data-det>
          <option value="fixed2" selected>Fixed timeout 2 s</option>
          <option value="fixed5">Fixed timeout 5 s</option>
          <option value="fixed10">Fixed timeout 10 s</option>
          <option value="phi4">Phi accrual, threshold 4</option>
          <option value="phi8">Phi accrual, threshold 8</option>
          <option value="phi12">Phi accrual, threshold 12</option>
          <option value="swim2">SWIM, 2 s suspicion</option>
          <option value="swim5">SWIM, 5 s suspicion</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Jitter
        <select class="pg-in" data-jit>
          <option value="low">Low (quiet LAN)</option>
          <option value="medium">Medium (1.5% delay spikes)</option>
          <option value="high" selected>High (5% delay spikes)</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Blip reaches
        <select class="pg-in" data-scope>
          <option value="link" selected>the monitor's link only</option>
          <option value="segment">the whole segment</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Trace seed <input class="pg-in fd-seed" type="number" min="1" max="999" value="1" data-seed /></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <button class="btn pg-primary" type="button" data-play>Play</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-step>Step +5 s</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
      <label class="fd-scrub">Playhead <input type="range" min="0" max="1600" value="0" step="1" data-head aria-label="Playhead time in tenths of a second" /></label>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-now aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="fd-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Timeline chart, scrolls sideways on narrow screens">
      <svg class="fd-svg" viewBox="0 0 600 220" role="img" aria-label="Timeline: heartbeat arrivals, suspicion value, and detector verdicts over 160 seconds" data-tl></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>Crash detected after</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-detect>-</span><span class="pg-note">measured from the last heartbeat (or ack) the monitor saw</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--bad)"><h3>False alarms</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-fp>-</span><span class="pg-note" data-fpnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Suspicions raised</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-raised>-</span><span class="pg-note" data-raisednote></span></div>
    </div>
    <h3 class="fd-h">Trade-off: detection time against false alarms</h3>
    <div class="fd-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Trade-off chart, scrolls sideways on narrow screens">
      <svg class="fd-svg" viewBox="0 0 600 210" role="img" aria-label="Scatter of detection time against number of false alarms for fixed timeouts, phi thresholds and SWIM suspicion timeouts" data-to></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="fd-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Comparison table, scrolls sideways on narrow screens">
      <table class="fd-table" data-table>
        <caption class="sr">All detectors on the current trace</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Detector</th><th scope="col">Crash found after</th><th scope="col">False alarms</th><th scope="col">GC pause</th><th scope="col">Blip</th><th scope="col">Jitter or warm-up</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note">Model assumptions: heartbeat every 1000 ms; one-way delay 20 ms plus jitter (5 / 20 / 50 ms times the sum of four uniforms), plus a 0.4 to 2.4 s spike with probability 0 / 1.5% / 5%. Phi uses a 100-sample window seeded with 750 and 1250 ms, a 100 ms floor on the standard deviation and the logistic approximation Akka uses. The monitor checks every 100 ms. SWIM probes once per second with a 500 ms direct timeout, then 3 indirect probes; a failed round makes the node suspect one second later. A paused or crashed node answers nobody; the target answers a probe after the pause, which refutes the suspicion. A false alarm is a verdict that a later heartbeat contradicts. Your own network will have heavier tails than this one, and a well-chosen fixed timeout (3 s here) happens to do as well as phi on this single trace: phi's advantage is that it finds that number for itself on every link.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  // ---- Pure simulation core (no DOM). Integer milliseconds throughout. ----
  const END = 160000; const CRASH_BEAT = 140; const CRASH_MS = 140000;
  const PAUSE_BEATS: [number, number] = [60, 65]; const BLIP_BEATS: [number, number] = [100, 104];
  const PAUSE_MS: [number, number] = [60000, 65000]; const BLIP_MS: [number, number] = [100000, 104000];
  const LEVELS: Record<string, { j: number; sp: number }> = { low: { j: 5, sp: 0 }, medium: { j: 20, sp: 15 }, high: { j: 50, sp: 50 } };
  type Cls = 'pause' | 'blip' | 'other';
  interface Span { start: number; verdictAt: number; clearedAt: number; falseAlarm: boolean }
  interface Result { contacts: number[]; score: number[]; spans: Span[]; fp: number; fpBy: Record<Cls, number>; detect: number; raised: number; refuted: number }

  function lcg(seed: number) {
    let s = seed >>> 0;
    return () => { s = (Math.imul(s, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0; return s >>> 16; };
  }
  function genTrace(seed: number, lv: string): number[] {
    const next = lcg(seed * 7919 + 13); const { j, sp } = LEVELS[lv]; const arr: number[] = [];
    for (let k = 0; k < CRASH_BEAT; k++) {
      const a = (next() % 1000) + (next() % 1000) + (next() % 1000) + (next() % 1000);
      const s = next() % 1000; const x = next() % 2000; const l = next() % 1000;
      if (k >= PAUSE_BEATS[0] && k < PAUSE_BEATS[1]) continue;
      if (k >= BLIP_BEATS[0] && k < BLIP_BEATS[1] && l < 700) continue;
      let d = 20 + Math.floor((j * a) / 1000); if (s < sp) d += 400 + x;
      arr.push(1000 * k + d);
    }
    return arr.sort((p, q) => p - q);
  }
  function classify(t: number): Cls {
    if (t >= PAUSE_MS[0] && t < PAUSE_MS[1] + 2000) return 'pause';
    if (t >= BLIP_MS[0] && t < BLIP_MS[1] + 3000) return 'blip';
    return 'other';
  }
  function finish(contacts: number[], score: number[], spans: Span[], detect: number, raised: number, refuted: number): Result {
    const fpBy: Record<Cls, number> = { pause: 0, blip: 0, other: 0 }; let fp = 0;
    spans.forEach((s) => { if (s.falseAlarm) { fp++; fpBy[classify(s.verdictAt)]++; } });
    return { contacts, score, spans, fp, fpBy, detect, raised, refuted };
  }
  // Fixed timeout or phi accrual over the arrival times.
  function runHeartbeat(arr: number[], kind: 'fixed' | 'phi', param: number): Result {
    const buf = [750, 1250]; let sum = 2000; let sq = 750 * 750 + 1250 * 1250;
    let ai = 0; let last = -1; let open: Span | null = null; const spans: Span[] = []; const score: number[] = [];
    for (let t = 0; t <= END; t += 100) {
      while (ai < arr.length && arr[ai] <= t) {
        if (last >= 0) { const iv = arr[ai] - last; buf.push(iv); sum += iv; sq += iv * iv; if (buf.length > 100) { const o = buf.shift()!; sum -= o; sq -= o * o; } }
        last = arr[ai++];
        if (open) { open.clearedAt = t; open.falseAlarm = true; open = null; }
      }
      if (last < 0) { score.push(0); continue; }
      const diff = t - last; let v: number; let bad: boolean;
      if (kind === 'fixed') { v = diff / param; bad = diff > param; }
      else {
        const n = buf.length; const m = sum / n; const sd = Math.max(Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, sq / n - m * m)), 100);
        const y = (diff - m) / sd; const e = Math.exp(-y * (1.5976 + 0.070566 * y * y));
        const p = diff > m ? e / (1 + e) : 1 - 1 / (1 + e);
        const phi = p < 1e-16 ? 16 : -Math.log10(p); v = phi / param; bad = phi >= param;
      }
      score.push(Math.min(v, 1.5));
      if (bad && !open) { open = { start: t, verdictAt: t, clearedAt: -1, falseAlarm: false }; spans.push(open); }
    }
    const detect = open ? open.start - last : -1;
    return finish(arr.slice(), score, spans, detect, spans.length, 0);
  }
  // SWIM-style probing: direct ping, 3 indirect probes, suspicion timer, refutation by the target.
  function runSwim(seed: number, lv: string, S: number, scope: string): Result {
    const r = lcg(seed * 104729 + 5); const { j, sp } = LEVELS[lv];
    const leg = () => { const a = (r() % 1000) + (r() % 1000) + (r() % 1000) + (r() % 1000); const s = r() % 1000; const x = r() % 2000; return 20 + Math.floor((j * a) / 1000) + (s < sp ? 400 + x : 0); };
    const score = new Array<number>(END / 100 + 1).fill(0); const spans: Span[] = []; const contacts: number[] = [];
    let open: Span | null = null; let lastOk = 0; let detect = -1; let raised = 0; let refuted = 0;
    const ramp = (a: number, b: number) => { for (let t = a; t <= b && t <= END; t += 100) score[t / 100] = Math.min(1, (t - a) / S); };
    for (let rd = 1; rd * 1000 <= END; rd++) {
      const tr = rd * 1000; const loss = r() % 1000; const d1 = leg(); const d2 = leg(); const il: number[] = [];
      for (let p = 0; p < 3; p++) il.push(leg() + leg() + leg() + leg());
      const up = tr < CRASH_MS && !(tr >= PAUSE_MS[0] && tr < PAUSE_MS[1]);
      const inBlip = tr >= BLIP_MS[0] && tr < BLIP_MS[1];
      const direct = !(inBlip && loss < 700) && d1 + d2 <= 500;
      const indirect = !(inBlip && scope === 'segment') && il.some((x) => x <= 500);
      const ok = up && (direct || indirect);
      if (open && open.verdictAt < 0 && tr >= open.start + S) {
        open.verdictAt = open.start + S; ramp(open.start, open.verdictAt);
        if (open.verdictAt < CRASH_MS) open.falseAlarm = true; else detect = open.verdictAt - lastOk;
      }
      if (ok) {
        contacts.push(tr); lastOk = tr;
        if (open) { if (open.verdictAt < 0) { refuted++; ramp(open.start, tr); } open.clearedAt = tr; open = null; }
      } else if (!open) { open = { start: tr + 1000, verdictAt: -1, clearedAt: -1, falseAlarm: false }; spans.push(open); raised++; }
    }
    return finish(contacts, score, spans, detect, raised, refuted);
  }
  interface Choice { id: string; label: string; kind: 'fixed' | 'phi' | 'swim'; param: number }
  const CHOICES: Choice[] = [
    { id: 'fixed2', label: 'Fixed timeout 2 s', kind: 'fixed', param: 2000 }, { id: 'fixed5', label: 'Fixed timeout 5 s', kind: 'fixed', param: 5000 },
    { id: 'fixed10', label: 'Fixed timeout 10 s', kind: 'fixed', param: 10000 }, { id: 'phi4', label: 'Phi accrual, threshold 4', kind: 'phi', param: 4 },
    { id: 'phi8', label: 'Phi accrual, threshold 8', kind: 'phi', param: 8 }, { id: 'phi12', label: 'Phi accrual, threshold 12', kind: 'phi', param: 12 },
    { id: 'swim2', label: 'SWIM, 2 s suspicion', kind: 'swim', param: 2000 }, { id: 'swim5', label: 'SWIM, 5 s suspicion', kind: 'swim', param: 5000 },
  ];
  function runChoice(c: Choice, arr: number[], seed: number, lv: string, scope: string): Result {
    return c.kind === 'swim' ? runSwim(seed, lv, c.param, scope) : runHeartbeat(arr, c.kind, c.param);
  }
  interface Point { x: number; y: number; param: number }
  function sweep(arr: number[], seed: number, lv: string, scope: string) {
    const fixed: Point[] = []; const phi: Point[] = []; const swim: Point[] = [];
    for (let T = 1000; T <= 12000; T += 500) { const r = runHeartbeat(arr, 'fixed', T); if (r.detect >= 0) fixed.push({ x: r.detect, y: r.fp, param: T }); }
    for (let p = 1; p <= 16; p++) { const r = runHeartbeat(arr, 'phi', p); if (r.detect >= 0) phi.push({ x: r.detect, y: r.fp, param: p }); }
    for (let S = 1000; S <= 10000; S += 1000) { const r = runSwim(seed, lv, S, scope); if (r.detect >= 0) swim.push({ x: r.detect, y: r.fp, param: S }); }
    return { fixed, phi, swim };
  }

  // ---- DOM ----
  const NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  function el(tag: string, attrs: Record<string, string | number>, parent?: Element, text?: string) {
    const n = document.createElementNS(NS, tag);
    Object.entries(attrs).forEach(([k, v]) => n.setAttribute(k, String(v)));
    if (text !== undefined) n.textContent = text;
    if (parent) parent.appendChild(n);
    return n;
  }
  const secs = (ms: number) => (ms / 1000).toFixed(1);

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fd]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends Element>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const reduce = typeof matchMedia === 'function' && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    const tl = q<SVGSVGElement>('[data-tl]'); const to = q<SVGSVGElement>('[data-to]');
    const X0 = 36; const X1 = 590; const tx = (ms: number) => X0 + ((X1 - X0) * ms) / END;
    const YB = 180; const ys = (v: number) => YB - 80 * Math.min(v, 1.5);
    let res: Result; let sw: ReturnType<typeof sweep>; let choice = CHOICES[0]; let playTimer: number | undefined; let onScreen = true; let raf = 0;
    let headTick = 0;

    // Timeline, built once.
    const band = (a: number, b: number, label: string, colour: string) => {
      el('rect', { x: tx(a), y: 14, width: tx(b) - tx(a), height: YB - 14, fill: colour, opacity: 0.16 }, tl);
      el('text', { x: tx(a) + 3, y: 11, 'font-size': 10, fill: 'var(--muted)' }, tl, label);
    };
    band(PAUSE_MS[0], PAUSE_MS[1], 'GC pause', 'var(--role-3)'); band(BLIP_MS[0], BLIP_MS[1], 'blip', 'var(--role-1)');
    el('line', { x1: tx(CRASH_MS), x2: tx(CRASH_MS), y1: 14, y2: YB, stroke: 'var(--bad)', 'stroke-width': 2 }, tl);
    el('text', { x: tx(CRASH_MS) + 3, y: 11, 'font-size': 10, fill: 'var(--muted)' }, tl, 'crash');
    el('line', { x1: X0, x2: X1, y1: ys(1), y2: ys(1), stroke: 'var(--bad)', 'stroke-dasharray': '5 4', 'stroke-width': 1 }, tl);
    el('text', { x: 2, y: ys(1) + 3, 'font-size': 9, fill: 'var(--muted)' }, tl, 'verdict');
    el('text', { x: 2, y: YB + 3, 'font-size': 9, fill: 'var(--muted)' }, tl, '0');
    el('line', { x1: X0, x2: X1, y1: YB, y2: YB, stroke: 'var(--border)' }, tl);
    for (let s = 0; s <= 160; s += 20) { el('line', { x1: tx(s * 1000), x2: tx(s * 1000), y1: YB, y2: YB + 4, stroke: 'var(--muted)' }, tl); el('text', { x: tx(s * 1000), y: YB + 15, 'font-size': 10, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: 'var(--muted)' }, tl, `${s}s`); }
    el('text', { x: X0, y: 214, 'font-size': 10, fill: 'var(--muted)' }, tl, 'ticks above the axis: heartbeats (or SWIM acks) seen by the monitor');
    const beats = el('path', { fill: 'none', stroke: 'var(--role-2)', 'stroke-width': 1 }, tl);
    const line = el('polyline', { fill: 'none', stroke: 'var(--accent)', 'stroke-width': 2 }, tl);
    const markers: { g: Element; c: Element; t: Element }[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < 40; i++) {
      const g = el('g', { visibility: 'hidden' }, tl); const c = el('circle', { r: 5, 'stroke-width': 2 }, g); const t = el('text', { 'font-size': 9, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: 'var(--text)' }, g);
      markers.push({ g, c, t });
    }
    const cursor = el('line', { y1: 14, y2: YB, stroke: 'var(--text)', 'stroke-width': 1 }, tl);

    // Trade-off chart, built once.
    const TX0 = 40; const TX1 = 580; const tox = (ms: number) => TX0 + ((TX1 - TX0) * Math.min(ms, 13000)) / 13000;
    const YMAX = 8; const toy = (n: number) => 170 - (150 * Math.min(n, YMAX)) / YMAX;
    el('line', { x1: TX0, x2: TX1, y1: 170, y2: 170, stroke: 'var(--border)' }, to); el('line', { x1: TX0, x2: TX0, y1: 20, y2: 170, stroke: 'var(--border)' }, to);
    for (let s = 0; s <= 12; s += 2) { el('text', { x: tox(s * 1000), y: 186, 'font-size': 10, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: 'var(--muted)' }, to, `${s}s`); }
    for (let n = 0; n <= YMAX; n += 2) { el('text', { x: TX0 - 6, y: toy(n) + 3, 'font-size': 10, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: 'var(--muted)' }, to, n === YMAX ? `${n}+` : String(n)); }
    el('text', { x: (TX0 + TX1) / 2, y: 204, 'font-size': 10, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: 'var(--muted)' }, to, 'time to detect the crash (lower is better)');
    el('text', { x: 12, y: 95, 'font-size': 10, fill: 'var(--muted)', transform: 'rotate(-90 12 95)', 'text-anchor': 'middle' }, to, 'false alarms');
    const series = [
      { key: 'fixed' as const, colour: 'var(--role-1)', dash: '', name: 'fixed timeout (1 to 12 s)', lx: 330 },
      { key: 'phi' as const, colour: 'var(--role-2)', dash: '6 3', name: 'phi (threshold 1 to 16)', lx: 330 },
      { key: 'swim' as const, colour: 'var(--role-3)', dash: '2 3', name: 'SWIM (suspicion 1 to 10 s)', lx: 330 },
    ];
    const lines = series.map((s, i) => {
      el('line', { x1: 440, x2: 466, y1: 32 + i * 14, y2: 32 + i * 14, stroke: s.colour, 'stroke-width': 2, 'stroke-dasharray': s.dash }, to);
      el('text', { x: 472, y: 35 + i * 14, 'font-size': 10, fill: 'var(--text)' }, to, s.name);
      return el('polyline', { fill: 'none', stroke: s.colour, 'stroke-width': 2, 'stroke-dasharray': s.dash }, to);
    });
    const selRing = el('circle', { r: 8, fill: 'none', stroke: 'var(--text)', 'stroke-width': 2 }, to);
    const selText = el('text', { 'font-size': 10, fill: 'var(--text)' }, to);

    // Table, built once.
    const tbody = q<HTMLElement>('[data-table] tbody'); const rows: HTMLTableRowElement[] = [];
    CHOICES.forEach(() => { const tr = document.createElement('tr'); for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) tr.appendChild(document.createElement('td')); tbody.appendChild(tr); rows.push(tr); });

    function stateAt(ms: number) {
      for (const s of res.spans) {
        const end = s.clearedAt >= 0 ? s.clearedAt : END + 1;
        if (ms >= s.start && ms < end) return s.verdictAt >= 0 && ms >= s.verdictAt ? 'DEAD verdict' : 'SUSPECT, grace timer running';
      }
      return 'ALIVE';
    }
    function drawCursor() {
      const ms = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-head]').value) * 100;
      cursor.setAttribute('x1', String(tx(ms))); cursor.setAttribute('x2', String(tx(ms)));
      let last = -1; for (let i = 0; i < res.contacts.length && res.contacts[i] <= ms; i++) last = res.contacts[i];
      const v = res.score[Math.min(res.score.length - 1, Math.floor(ms / 100))];
      const what = choice.kind === 'swim' ? 'progress of suspicion timer' : choice.kind === 'phi' ? `phi ${(v * choice.param).toFixed(1)} of ${choice.param}` : `silence ${last >= 0 ? secs(ms - last) : '-'} s of ${secs(choice.param)} s`;
      q('[data-now]').textContent = `t = ${secs(ms)} s | last ${choice.kind === 'swim' ? 'ack' : 'heartbeat'}: ${last >= 0 ? `${secs(ms - last)} s ago` : 'none yet'} | ${what} (${(v * 100).toFixed(0)}% of verdict) | state: ${stateAt(ms)}`;
    }
    function draw() {
      const lv = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-jit]').value;
      // beats
      let d = ''; res.contacts.forEach((c) => { d += `M${tx(c).toFixed(1)} ${YB - 14}V${YB - 2}`; }); beats.setAttribute('d', d);
      line.setAttribute('points', res.score.map((v, i) => `${tx(i * 100).toFixed(1)},${ys(v).toFixed(1)}`).join(' '));
      markers.forEach((m, i) => {
        const s = res.spans[i];
        if (!s) { m.g.setAttribute('visibility', 'hidden'); return; }
        const t = s.verdictAt >= 0 ? s.verdictAt : s.start; const isFalse = s.falseAlarm || (s.verdictAt < 0 && s.clearedAt >= 0);
        const raisedOnly = s.verdictAt < 0;
        m.g.setAttribute('visibility', 'visible'); m.g.setAttribute('transform', `translate(${tx(t).toFixed(1)} ${ys(raisedOnly ? 0.3 : 1).toFixed(1)})`);
        m.c.setAttribute('fill', raisedOnly ? 'var(--surface)' : isFalse ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--text)');
        m.c.setAttribute('stroke', raisedOnly ? 'var(--muted)' : 'var(--bad)');
        m.t.setAttribute('y', '-8'); m.t.textContent = raisedOnly ? 'refuted' : isFalse ? 'false' : 'dead';
      });
      // stats
      q('[data-detect]').textContent = res.detect >= 0 ? `${(res.detect / 1000).toFixed(2)} s` : 'not detected';
      q('[data-fp]').textContent = String(res.fp);
      q('[data-fpnote]').textContent = `GC pause: ${res.fpBy.pause} | blip: ${res.fpBy.blip} | jitter or warm-up: ${res.fpBy.other}`;
      q('[data-raised]').textContent = String(res.raised);
      q('[data-raisednote]').textContent = choice.kind === 'swim' ? `${res.refuted} cleared by the target's refutation before the timer ran out` : 'no grace period: every suspicion is a verdict';
      // trade-off
      series.forEach((s, i) => { lines[i].setAttribute('points', sw[s.key].map((p) => `${tox(p.x).toFixed(1)},${toy(p.y).toFixed(1)}`).join(' ')); });
      if (res.detect >= 0) { selRing.setAttribute('visibility', 'visible'); selRing.setAttribute('cx', tox(res.detect).toFixed(1)); selRing.setAttribute('cy', toy(res.fp).toFixed(1)); selText.setAttribute('visibility', 'visible'); selText.setAttribute('x', String(Math.min(tox(res.detect) + 10, 520))); selText.setAttribute('y', (toy(res.fp) - 10).toFixed(1)); selText.textContent = `selected: ${res.fp} false, ${secs(res.detect)} s`; }
      else { selRing.setAttribute('visibility', 'hidden'); selText.setAttribute('visibility', 'hidden'); }
      // table
      CHOICES.forEach((c, i) => {
        const r = c.id === choice.id ? res : runChoice(c, trace, Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]').value), lv, q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-scope]').value);
        const cells = rows[i].children; cells[0].textContent = c.label; cells[1].textContent = r.detect >= 0 ? `${(r.detect / 1000).toFixed(2)} s` : 'not detected';
        cells[2].textContent = String(r.fp); cells[3].textContent = String(r.fpBy.pause); cells[4].textContent = String(r.fpBy.blip); cells[5].textContent = String(r.fpBy.other);
        rows[i].style.fontWeight = c.id === choice.id ? '700' : '400';
      });
      drawCursor();
    }
    let trace: number[] = [];
    function recompute() {
      const lv = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-jit]').value; const scope = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-scope]').value;
      const seed = Math.max(1, Math.min(999, Math.floor(Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]').value) || 1)));
      choice = CHOICES.find((c) => c.id === q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-det]').value) || CHOICES[0];
      trace = genTrace(seed, lv); res = runChoice(choice, trace, seed, lv, scope); sw = sweep(trace, seed, lv, scope);
      draw();
    }
    function schedule() { if (raf) return; raf = requestAnimationFrame(() => { raf = 0; drawCursor(); }); }
    function setHead(v: number) { q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-head]').value = String(Math.max(0, Math.min(1600, v))); schedule(); }
    function stop() { if (playTimer !== undefined) { window.clearInterval(playTimer); playTimer = undefined; } q('[data-play]').textContent = 'Play'; }
    function play() {
      stop(); if (reduce || !onScreen || document.hidden) return;
      q('[data-play]').textContent = 'Pause';
      playTimer = window.setInterval(() => {
        headTick = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-head]').value) + 10;
        if (headTick >= 1600) { setHead(1600); stop(); return; }
        setHead(headTick);
      }, 100);
    }
    ['[data-det]', '[data-jit]', '[data-scope]', '[data-seed]'].forEach((s) => q(s).addEventListener('change', recompute));
    q('[data-head]').addEventListener('input', () => { stop(); schedule(); });
    q('[data-play]').addEventListener('click', () => { if (playTimer !== undefined) stop(); else { if (Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-head]').value) >= 1600) setHead(0); play(); } });
    q('[data-step]').addEventListener('click', () => { stop(); setHead(Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-head]').value) + 50); });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => { stop(); q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-det]').value = 'fixed2'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-jit]').value = 'high'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-scope]').value = 'link'; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]').value = '1'; setHead(0); recompute(); });
    if (reduce) { const b = q<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-play]'); b.disabled = true; b.title = 'Disabled because you prefer reduced motion; use Step or the Playhead'; }
    if (typeof IntersectionObserver === 'function') new IntersectionObserver(([en]) => { onScreen = en.isIntersecting; if (!onScreen) stop(); }).observe(root);
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => { if (document.hidden) stop(); });
    recompute();
  });
</script>
